{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "C64 Shell ROM + Stock Fallback",
 "description": "Shell ROM + stock C64 BASIC/KERNAL fallback + a character ROM served on a 3rd chip-select (the char socket /CS), switchable between two fonts. Loadable ROM sets: 0 = shell KERNAL+BASIC+charset (boot), 1 = stock+charset, 2/3 = overlays_a/b, 4 = shell KERNAL+BASIC+swedish (font B), 5 = overlays_c (appended so font B's set index stays 4). The `font` command live-switches the char ROM via RBCP SWITCH_SLOT (sets 0<->4 carry identical KERNAL/BASIC, so only the font changes). Overlay sets carry the same 8KB image on all three chips: firmware 0.7.x sizes RAM slots to the served (multi-ROM) type and LOAD_SLOT refuses a size mismatch, so single-ROM sets no longer load while a multi-ROM set is served -- tripling them makes every set the same multi-ROM size (Piers' workaround, hardware-validated on 0.7.1; a proper single-into-multi primitive may come in 0.7.2).",
